b1nix kernel headers
====================

These are the headers and build files for one b1nix kernel release, installed
under /usr/src/b1nix-headers-<release>.

They exist so that a module can be built against this kernel. They are not a
statement that any particular out-of-tree module works: Debian's DKMS packages
(nvidia, virtualbox, zfs and the rest) are written against Linux, and b1nix is
not Linux. Expect them to fail to build, and do not report that as a bug unless
the failure is in something b1nix claims to provide.

What is supported is building modules that are written for b1nix, against the
release whose headers these are. A module built against one release does not
load into another: the release string is part of the module's vermagic, and a
mismatch is refused rather than risked.
